cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "peps-pipeline v3: a reproducible peptidome prediction pipeline"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ortega-Batista
    given-names: Ana Cristina
    affiliation: Universidad Tecnologica de Panama
    email: ana.ortega6@utp.ac.pa
version: 3.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/pepperandhoney/peps-pipeline"
abstract: >-
  Docker-based pipeline for large-scale MHC-I and MHC-II peptide binding
  prediction. Protein identifiers are renumbered to survive the 15-character
  header truncation applied by NetMHCpan and restored after parsing, so the
  protein of origin is never lost. Version 3 adds multilength campaigns, a
  massive-batch mode built on GNU Parallel, and a shared library that gives
  every stage the same conventions.
